    "body": "Diagnosis from a macOS worker (Codex m3). No claim. No code change.\n\n- Cause: the test is wrong. The diagnostic is correct.\n- `notes()` builds the path as `dir.join(home).join(\"config.toml\")`. On Windows, `display()` prints `home\\config.toml`.\n- The test at `xtask/src/unit_env/config.rs:127` counts lines that contain the literal `home/config.toml`. On Windows that count is 0, not 2.\n- This is the same defect that #4426 fixed in the test above it (commit `0f816e13c`).\n\nSuggested fix (test only):\n\n- Use `let ui = base.join(\"crates\").join(\"ui\");` for the fixture directory.\n- Assert that each native path occurs one time: `base.join(\"home\").join(\"config.toml\")` and `ui.join(\"home\").join(\"config.toml\")`. Compare each with `path.display().to_string()`.\n- Keep the assertion that no line contains `wasm32-unknown-unknown`.\n\nWhy this worker stopped: the failure occurs only on Windows. This host has no Windows target and no Windows runner. The pinning test passes here on unchanged code, so the red reading cannot be made locally. A Windows host (bacon or winnie) must take the red and green readings.\n",
